From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:55:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] MdeModulePkg/Ps2MouseDxe: Report at 100 Hz and 8
 counts/mm, keep in sync

The driver sets the mouse to 20 reports per second at 4 counts/mm, and
takes one packet per 10 ms poll. On a laptop the TrackPoint and the
touchpad come through this driver, and at 20 reports per second the
pointer moves in steps of whatever the finger did in 50 ms; the pad,
which filters its own motion for a 100 Hz host, responds poorly too.

Set 100 reports per second at 8 counts/mm, the settings operating
systems use, and take every packet that is waiting at each poll, up to
eight, so that a delayed poll does not leave them queued in the device.

The first byte of a packet was recognized by bit 3 set and bit 2 clear:
bit 2 is the middle button, so a packet with it pressed (the TrackPoint
scrolls with it) was not a packet, and the driver read its data bytes as
first bytes until it happened to find one, with the motion of the bytes
in between applied as it came. Recognize the first byte by bit 3 set and
the overflow bits 6 and 7 clear instead: the buttons may be pressed, and
the data bytes of a lost packet are rejected seven times out of eight
rather than three out of four.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/CommPs2.h  | 16 +++++++++++--
 MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/Ps2Mouse.c | 26 +++++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/CommPs2.h b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/CommPs2.h
index d6fc0cc8c7..769823b390 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/CommPs2.h
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/CommPs2.h
@@ -11,8 +11,20 @@ SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
 #include "Ps2Mouse.h"
 
 #define PS2_PACKET_LENGTH  3
-#define PS2_SYNC_MASK      0xc
-#define PS2_SYNC_BYTE      0x8
+
+//
+// The first byte of a packet has bit 3 set and, unless the device reports
+// more motion than a packet holds (never at these settings, and nothing to
+// move the pointer by), the overflow bits 6 and 7 clear. The buttons, bits
+// 0 to 2, may be pressed: a packet with the middle button down is a packet.
+//
+#define PS2_SYNC_MASK      0xc8
+#define PS2_SYNC_BYTE      0x08
+
+//
+// Packets taken per poll of the device
+//
+#define PS2_PACKETS_PER_POLL  8
 
 #define IS_PS2_SYNC_BYTE(byte)  ((byte & PS2_SYNC_MASK) == PS2_SYNC_BYTE)
 
diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/Ps2Mouse.c b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/Ps2Mouse.c
index fb61f75e08..84aa63d627 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/Ps2Mouse.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Isa/Ps2MouseDxe/Ps2Mouse.c
@@ -218,17 +218,22 @@ PS2MouseDriverStart (
   //
   MouseDev->Signature       = PS2_MOUSE_DEV_SIGNATURE;
   MouseDev->Handle          = Controller;
-  MouseDev->SampleRate      = SampleRate20;
-  MouseDev->Resolution      = MouseResolution4;
+  //
+  // 100 reports per second at 8 counts/mm, the settings operating systems
+  // use: at 20 reports per second the pointer moves in steps, and the
+  // pads of laptops, which process their own motion, respond poorly.
+  //
+  MouseDev->SampleRate      = SampleRate100;
+  MouseDev->Resolution      = MouseResolution8;
   MouseDev->Scaling         = Scaling1;
   MouseDev->DataPackageSize = 3;
   MouseDev->DevicePath      = DevicePath;
 
   //
-  // Resolution = 4 counts/mm
+  // Resolution = 8 counts/mm
   //
-  MouseDev->Mode.ResolutionX = 4;
-  MouseDev->Mode.ResolutionY = 4;
+  MouseDev->Mode.ResolutionX = 8;
+  MouseDev->Mode.ResolutionY = 8;
   MouseDev->Mode.LeftButton  = TRUE;
   MouseDev->Mode.RightButton = TRUE;
 
@@ -757,13 +762,20 @@ PollMouse (
 
 {
   PS2_MOUSE_DEV  *MouseDev;
+  UINTN          Count;
 
   MouseDev = (PS2_MOUSE_DEV *)Context;
 
   //
-  // Polling mouse packet data
+  // Polling mouse packet data. Take every packet that is already waiting,
+  // not only the first: at 100 reports per second a delayed poll finds more
+  // than one, and they would queue up in the device.
   //
-  PS2MouseGetPacket (MouseDev);
+  for (Count = 0; Count < PS2_PACKETS_PER_POLL; Count++) {
+    if (EFI_ERROR (PS2MouseGetPacket (MouseDev))) {
+      break;
+    }
+  }
 }
 
